{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{
  "summary": "Add a dependency-free title-to-slug helper, with the supported Unicode folding scope made explicit.",
  "stories": [
    {
      "id": "blog-author",
      "who": "A blog author",
      "want": "A URL slug made from a post title",
      "why": "Titles with spaces, punctuation and accented letters need a consistent URL form.",
      "from": null
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "title": "Add title-to-slug conversion",
      "ends": "pr",
      "job": {
        "when": "A blog author converts three post titles for publication",
        "result": "“Hello, World!” becomes “hello-world”, “Çay Şeker” becomes “cay-seker”, and “!!!” becomes an empty string.",
        "check": {
          "how": "test",
          "what": "Compare the three title-to-slug results with the expected strings."
        },
        "serves": ["blog-author"],
        "fixture": "One batch of three titles, converted once each: an English greeting, a Turkish title with accents, and punctuation without usable text."
      },
      "criteria": [
        {
          "when": "A developer reads the public helper documentation",
          "result": "The documentation explains the chosen folding scope, including what happens to letters without a supported ASCII form.",
          "check": {
            "how": "read",
            "what": "Read the helper’s public documentation and compare its folding examples with the resolved folding decision."
          },
          "serves": ["blog-author"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "goal": null,
  "pointers": [
    {
      "at": "src/slug.ts",
      "why": "The title-to-slug task owns this new file, its named slugify export and its public documentation."
    },
    {
      "at": "src/slug.test.ts",
      "why": "The title-to-slug task owns the adjacent tests for all planned properties."
    },
    {
      "at": "src/title.ts and src/title.test.ts",
      "why": "Existing examples establish named exports, direct TypeScript imports and adjacent Vitest tests."
    },
    {
      "at": "AGENTS.md and README.md",
      "why": "Repository notes require one file per helper, adjacent tests and no runtime dependencies; fast-check is available."
    },
    {
      "at": ".fabrika/fabrika.toml, package.json and tsconfig.json",
      "why": "Existing test and typecheck configuration supports this task without exam changes."
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "ask": "How broadly should non-ASCII letters fold into ASCII?",
      "options": [
        "Use Unicode compatibility decomposition and remove combining marks; remaining non-ASCII characters separate words.",
        "Also support an explicitly agreed transliteration table for letters such as ß, æ and ø."
      ],
      "lean": "Use Unicode compatibility decomposition and remove combining marks. This gives Çay Şeker → cay-seker and ﬂower → flower, but Straße → stra-e.",
      "why": "“When they can” does not define a complete folding policy. The folding property, unsupported-character property and documentation criterion depend on this choice.",
      "cost": "The lean gives bounded behavior without a maintained mapping table; broader transliteration needs an agreed character set and additional examples.",
      "sure": 75,
      "doubt": "Confirm whether titles containing letters such as ß, æ and ø must retain their usual transliterations."
    }
  ],
  "properties": [
    {
      "when": "The three publication titles are converted",
      "result": "Their slugs are respectively “hello-world”, “cay-seker” and an empty string.",
      "why": "This is the author’s first useful workflow; it fails today because the slug helper does not exist.",
      "behavior": "new",
      "tool": "test",
      "code": []
    },
    {
      "when": "Nonempty ASCII letter-and-digit words are joined by spaces and converted",
      "result": "The slug is exactly the original words lowercased and joined by one hyphen, preserving every digit and letter in order.",
      "why": "Dropping usable content would change the title’s meaning in its URL; the new helper is absent today.",
      "behavior": "new",
      "tool": "test",
      "code": []
    },
    {
      "when": "Accented and compatibility-form titles such as “Çay Şeker”, “Café” and “ﬂower”, including their decomposed accent spellings, are converted",
      "result": "They produce “cay-seker”, “cafe” and “flower” respectively.",
      "why": "Equivalent accent spellings should retain their readable letters; these cases fail today because the helper is absent. Compatibility folding follows the proposed decision.",
      "behavior": "new",
      "tool": "test",
      "code": []
    },
    {
      "when": "Usable words are surrounded or separated by runs of whitespace, punctuation, emoji or characters still unsupported after folding",
      "result": "Each internal separator run becomes one hyphen and edge separators disappear, including “  Tea__&🍵Cake!  ” → “tea-cake” and “a中b” → “a-b”.",
      "why": "Deleting unsupported characters could incorrectly merge words; the helper is absent today. Which characters remain unsupported depends on the folding decision.",
      "behavior": "new",
      "tool": "test",
      "code": []
    },
    {
      "when": "A title is empty or contains only whitespace, punctuation, emoji or unsupported characters",
      "result": "Its slug is an empty string.",
      "why": "A title without usable content must not produce a separator-only slug; this behavior is absent today.",
      "behavior": "new",
      "tool": "test",
      "code": []
    },
    {
      "when": "Any generated Unicode title is converted",
      "result": "The output is empty or consists solely of lowercase ASCII letter-and-digit groups separated by single hyphens.",
      "why": "Unexpected Unicode input must not leak unsupported characters or malformed separators into URLs; the new helper is absent today.",
      "behavior": "new",
      "tool": "test",
      "code": []
    }
  ],
  "interface": "```typescript\nexport declare function slugify(text: string): string;\n```",
  "exam": [],
  "gaps": [
    "The brief does not define the extent of Unicode folding. This blocks a definitive transliteration expectation; the plan uses the stated lean and records the decision as a question.",
    "The supplied folder has no Git metadata, so its commit identity and note chronology could not be independently verified. All available repository notes were read, no clashes were found, and the supplied snapshot was treated as the stated baseline."
  ]
}"}}
